Hyphenate the Syllables: Break the word down into individual syllables using hyphens to slow it down dramatically.
Example: s-l-o-w-l-y or wa-ter-fall.
Use Extra Vowels: Draw out the word by adding more vowels.
Example: ho~me or faaaast.
Add Ellipses or Spaces: Place periods or spaces between letters or words to create a pause before or within the word.
Example: Wait... for it or S p e a k.
Capitalization for Emphasis: Use ALL CAPS to emphasize a word, which often causes Suno to draw it out.
Example: He ran SLOWLY.
Add [Pause] or [Slow] Tags: Place structural tags before the word.
Example: [pause] home.
Use Phonetic Spelling: Spell the word how it sounds, not how it is spelled, to force a slower cadence
